{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/53171-intercepted-messages","id":53171,"title":"Intercepted Messages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-19T07:12:08-08:00","id":53171,"title":"Intercepted Messages","content":"Spies send and receive messages. Sometimes, they intercept something they were not meant to get. Should they act upon the knowledge they just acquired, or should they just run away from the consequences? Who sent it to whom? What if it's a trap? Can they arrange to send it again without betraying the fact it was tempered with, or is it something they don't have to worry about (due to it being broadcast for example)? Do they have hours or days to act, or is it a race against time, as the original recipient received it at the same time? Or perhaps they received it long ago already? Is the message clear and unambiguous, or could they be missing a key element?<br /> I'd like to know what such messages a Demon could intercept, on purpose or (seemingly) by chance.<br /> <br /> <br /> My own contribution to start:<br /> Bees dance to communicate. That is well-known. But this time, their dance is bizarre. They draw out letters and numbers lasting a split second in the air. It says, &quot;Gate open 01 22 14&quot;. The buzzing of their wings, meanwhile, screams &quot;HERE&quot;. You turn around. Many other people are admiring the floral garden. You turn again. The swarm lands on the flowers, dying, but people do not react, thinking.they're simply gathering pollen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T20:52:10-08:00","id":54456,"title":"","content":"You (now) go to a local piano bar on a regular basis. Every night, no matter what musician or song is playing or what the crowd in the room is made up of, the audience blinks a repeating pattern out with their eyes that only the musician could see with total perspective. You latched on this the night you put a tip in the jar on top of the piano and momentarily saw a fragment in the sum total of presenting faces for a split second when you turned around to walk back to your seat.<br /> <br /> Now, you tip every night you're there and make drunken excuses for a lengthy stagger back to your seat so you can glimpse at the message over and over until you get further clarity on its meaning. The barstaff know your name now and you've felt your cover being eroded recently. It wasn't until last night that you got a first understanding of the coded message: &quot;honeytrap&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T16:26:50-08:00","id":56417,"title":"","content":"Experiencing the terrible awful vile element of the human condition known as &quot;boredom,&quot; you attempt to salve it: you paint a picture (it comes out gray and all wrong, one giant eyeball), you eat a pizza (three, one of which is guava and sardine, &quot;just to see what happens,&quot;), you go for a walk.<br /> On your jaunt, you see a car accident. You see another, but well, walking around New York City for two and a half hours, you think the odds are pretty good. You see a few more, and then you get to counting them: their frequency within the hour, how much time is spaced between them, why there come in clusters separated by half-hour intervals.<br /> You get back to your flat and pat your gecko on the head and write down the numbers you've been playing with.<br /> It seems a little off.<br /> <br /> It takes another week of watching and recording to notice that they are spelling something out in Morse Code, and by then you've only half the sentence: &quot;3 days stop the First will be in Atlanta, Georgia stop for -&quot;<br /> Do you wait for the rest, or do you rush down anyway?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","user":"Ben Quo","date":". 02-01-2014, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}